--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Friday, the 2nd of January, 1931 (0/4 key facts kept) ---
I was gloomy about the New Year, which has opened so gloomily, throwing more than two and a half million workers out of employment, and bringing disputes into the coal and cotton trades.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Friday, the 2nd of January, 1931 (5/5 key facts kept) ---
To-day I balanced the quarterly ledger, spoke with Mr. Walter Thomas about the gloomy prospects of the New Year, and was paid my week's wages, £3 10s.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Friday, the 2nd of January, 1931 (0/3 key facts kept) ---
I was sorry to read in The Times that the New Year opens gloomily, with more than two and a half million out of work and the coal and cotton trades in dispute.
