   ◇ Ada reflects: She thinks him a failure, because he has been refused employment.
   ◇ Ada reflects: She thinks him a scurvy trickster, because he has cheated her out of twelve shillings.
   ◇ Ada reflects: She thinks her a decent, needy person, to whom sixpence may properly be lent.
   ◇ Arthur reflects: He thinks him a cautious, quiet man, because he spoke to him about the weather and the state of the coal trade.
   ◇ Arthur reflects: She is thrifty, because she takes charge of the housekeeping on an income of thirty-five shillings a week.
   ◇ Mr. Thomas reflects: He thinks her a steady, respectable person, because she never missed a morning's work in twelve months.
   ◇ Mr. Thomas reflects: He thinks him a capable and industrious young clerk, because he performed correctly the duties which were assigned to him, and because, when spoken to about the weather, he replied sensibly.
   📅 Ada means to: Monday: washes Bert's things, mend them, and gets him some shirts
   📅 Arthur means to: Monday: posts his books | Tuesday: buys coal | Wednesday: pays the rent | Thursday: gets himself a new pair of boots
   📅 Mr. Thomas means to: Monday: sees about getting a pair of boots soled

--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Sunday, the 4th of January, 1931 (1/4 key facts kept) ---
I am glad to have repaid Mr. Gedge his rent; I am glad to have received coals from Mrs. Nolan; I am sorry to have been asked for money by Mrs. Burrows.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Sunday, the 4th of January, 1931 (5/5 key facts kept) ---
To-day I balanced the quarterly ledger, and spoke to Walter Thomas about the gloomy New Year, and the coal and cotton trades.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Sunday, the 4th of January, 1931 (0/2 key facts kept) ---
Mr. Thomas was gloomy, and wondered how long he would have to pay wages to so many people who could get no work to do.
   ☾ Ada (forgotten by morning): She dreamt that she was standing at a baker's shop door in the Old Kent Road, and saw a pile of new rolls in the window.
   ☾ Arthur (forgotten by morning): He dreamt that he was an office boy again, in a little room off Cheapside, and saw himself promoted to be a junior clerk.
   ☾ Mr. Thomas (forgotten by morning): He dreamt that he saw the office perfectly clean.

