--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Monday, the 5th of January, 1931 (0/0 key facts kept) ---
I read in the evening paper that Princess Louise was dead, and that she had been seriously ill for some months. I was sorry to hear it, for the Princess was kind to me when I used to clean out the Moorgate offices, and I felt personal grief at her loss. I also read that Millwall had beaten Charlton at football, by six goals to nil, and I was glad, because Charlton had beaten Millwall the week before.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Monday, the 5th of January, 1931 (0/0 key facts kept) ---
I read in the Daily Herald the death of Princess Louise, and also that she had been seriously ill for some months. I was sorry to hear of her death, because she had always been kind to me, and I had hoped she would recover. Football: Millwall beat Charlton by six goals to nil, which was satisfactory to me, because Charlton had beaten Millwall in the previous match. Mrs. Turner has lost her place at the insurance office; I am sorry for her.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Monday, the 5th of January, 1931 (0/0 key facts kept) ---
I read in The Times of the death of the Princess Royal, and of increased weakness in Princess Louise. The office was not cleaned, and Mrs. Turner was given notice for not coming.
